ty  night  by first light i was already lying in no  man's land well camouflaged in the deep  snow  i was not concerned about concealment  but when i succeed in spotting the enemy  he would also be camouflaged against the  same snow one imagined just as well as i  was  and so i waited  however  it all turned out differently  suddenly i noticed against the pure  eye-testingly white snow a suspicious  little spot of something coloured  differently from snow had appeared and  thus while pondering and trying to  explain the reason for this spot i lost  sight of the most important thing the  thing i had been freezing so long for  but it all turned out to be very simple  beside this little spot on the surface a  big one suddenly appeared  in white camouflage  in a trace it crept up a couple of  meters to the left and disappeared as if  swallowed by the earth  from the unexpected nature of it all and  being chilled to the bone  i didn't even manage a shot  they literally carried me in their arms  to the dugout as my feet had refused to  move they were frozen and it appeared  frostbitten contact with hard surface  caused intolerable pain  but once again my friends came to the  rescue they took my footwear off in the  dugout and began to rub my feet with  snow and woolen gloves until i felt some  pin pricks the battalion medical  assistant was consulted  oh dear  no brains he said reproachfully you  should have smeared your feet with fat  before you went out wrap them in  newspaper and only then wound on your  foot wrappings  well i responded i'll do everything  scientifically tomorrow but today just  rub them make an effort to be a friend  in the morning i was awakened by the  company century  it's time up you get what already what a  pleasant dream you've interrupted i was  dreaming of my mother we were buying rye  flat cakes hot and fragrant  did you get to try one asked the century  he didn't give me a chance i answered  closing my eyes again enough betty bye  nicolaev you'll miss your nazi  that i was facing an experienced foe  there could be no doubt just as it could  not be doubted that he was already in  situ  he's outwitted me the bastard got there  earlier i thought when first light had  already dawned  tears began to form in my eyes from the  continuous observation of a single point  through telescopic sights it was the  wind blowing straight into my face and  the frost  i kept brushing away the tears while  trying not to make any obvious movements  the fingers of my right hand which were  constantly ready for action  had frozen and i began to worry as to  whether i would be able to hit the  target when necessary  i realized that in duels like this there  were no wounded  a sniper only ever makes a single  mistake  i had not taken a shot in over a week  and he had noticed that and was being  careful  i didn't have time to complete my  thought when suddenly something seemed  to prod me in the very heart and with  good reason the head of the nazi had  appeared from out of a trench above the  snowy covering all at once i felt hot  now just like yesterday he would drag  his large body out of the trench onto  the surface swiftly cover the three  meters distance and be off  no you must be joking you rat it won't  work this time and i firmly grasped the  rifle in my hands  the nazi's face firmly held in the  sights of my rifle was distinctly  visible through the eyepiece  he did not even glance in my direction i  had to bring him down and show everyone  that he was lying fallen on our land and  i was almost certain that any second now  he would leap out he was bound to repeat  his maneuver from yesterday only now i  knew about it and was expecting it  unsettled by the silence around and  hurried along by the intensifying frost  and gathering darkness with one short  jump the nazi landed up on the surface  of the ground stooping low he managed to  take his first  and last step  [Music]  the shot long awaited on our sector  resounded